# Shared Cycle Found Supabase project (same as cyclefound.com marketplace).
# Copy values from Cycle-Found-Website/.env.local:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL              → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# Server-only: community member directory (profiles are own-row RLS).
# Copy from Cycle-Found-Website/.env.local SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# Never expose as NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Server-only: AI photo identify + estimate fallback for Community garage items.
# Never expose this as NEXT_PUBLIC_*. Copy from Cycle-Found-Website/.env.local OPENAI_API_KEY.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides:
# OPENAI_VISION_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_ESTIMATE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Server-only: eBay Browse API (active listing / asking prices) for Get estimate.
# Uses client-credentials scope https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope — NOT Insights.
# Production App ID (Client ID) + Cert ID (Client Secret), not Sandbox.
# EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
# EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional:
# EBAY_CYCLING_CATEGORY_ID=177
# EBAY_MARKETPLACE_ID=EBAY_US
# EBAY_BROWSE_LIMIT=50

# Demo "Posting as" actor switch (Option A).
# Default: on in `next dev`, off in production builds.
# Set explicitly on Vercel when you need mock actors on a live URL:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_SESSION=1
# Force off locally:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_SESSION=0
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_SESSION=

# Insert Mock Data button in the Pre-Alpha banner.
# Default: off. Show locally with:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_MOCK_CONTROLS=1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_MOCK_CONTROLS=

# Optional Google Analytics 4 — loads only after Cookie settings “OK”.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Soft Pre-Alpha site gate (client-side only — not real security).
# When set, visitors must enter this password before seeing the app.
# Leave empty locally to skip the gate. Set on Vercel for the public demo:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_GATE_PASSWORD=your-invite-code
# Force off even if password is set: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_GATE=0

# Profiles handle migration (required for @handle identity):
#   Apply supabase/migrations/20261113090000_profiles_public_handle.sql
#   in the shared Supabase SQL editor before deploying Community handle work.
#
# Supabase Auth checklist (Dashboard → Authentication):
# 1. Email provider enabled (Sendit / custom SMTP already used by marketplace)
# 2. Enable Email OTP (6-digit codes) — Community is OTP-first
# 3. Magic Link email template MUST include {{ .Token }} or login emails
#    arrive with a link (or blank) and no 6-digit code. Community asks users
#    to type the code. Paste the branded HTML from docs/emails/magic-link.html
#    (logo: https://cyclefound.com/email/cycle-found-logo.png).
#    Dashboard → Authentication → Email Templates → Magic Link
#    Subject: Your Cycle Found sign-in code
# 4. Redirect URLs allowlist must include (apex cutover):
#    - http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#    - https://www.cyclefound.com/auth/callback
#    - https://cyclefound.com/auth/callback
#    - https://community.cyclefound.com/auth/callback  (keep during transition)
#    - https://classic.cyclefound.com/**               (archived marketplace)
#    Wildcards also work: https://www.cyclefound.com/**
#
# Google OAuth (Community + marketplace share one Supabase project):
# A. Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client (Web)
#    Authorized JavaScript origins:
#      - http://localhost:3000
#      - https://www.cyclefound.com
#      - https://cyclefound.com
#      - https://community.cyclefound.com  (keep during transition)
#      - https://classic.cyclefound.com
#    Authorized redirect URIs (THIS is Supabase’s callback — not the Community path):
#      - https://tvqrlgttfsalcxestdjp.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# B. Copy Client ID + Client Secret
# C. Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google → Enable
#    Paste Client ID + Secret → Save
# D. Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs (see list above)
#    Site URL should be https://www.cyclefound.com (Community) after cutover.
# E. Test: https://www.cyclefound.com/auth?mode=login → Continue with Google
#    Consent screen in “Testing”: add your Google account under Test users
# Docs: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/social-sign-in/auth-google
#
# Apple Sign in (web OAuth — Community already has Continue with Apple):
# A. Apple Developer → Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles
#    1. Identifiers → App IDs → create/edit App ID (e.g. com.cyclefound.app)
#       Enable capability: Sign in with Apple
#    2. Identifiers → Services IDs → Register (e.g. com.cyclefound.web)
#       Enable Sign in with Apple → Configure:
#         Primary App ID: the App ID from step 1
#         Domains: tvqrlgttfsalcxestdjp.supabase.co
#         Return URLs: https://tvqrlgttfsalcxestdjp.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#    3. Keys → Create a key → enable Sign in with Apple → link App ID → Download .p8
#       Note Key ID + Team ID (top-right of developer.apple.com)
# B. Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Apple → Enable
#    Client IDs: Services ID (com.cyclefound.web) — and App ID if you also do native later
#    Secret Key: generate JWT from Team ID + Key ID + .p8 (Supabase UI can help, or their docs)
#    → Save
# C. Same Redirect URLs allowlist as Google (see above). Site URL: https://www.cyclefound.com
# D. Test: https://www.cyclefound.com/auth?mode=join → Continue with Apple
# E. Rotate the Apple client secret every 6 months (Apple requirement) — calendar reminder
# Docs: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/social-sign-in/auth-apple
# Cutover runbook: docs/CUTOVER.md
